<title>UK: FORECAST - Results of Reuters survey of UK rates.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Results of Reuters survey of UK rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fifteen out of 20 economists surveyed by Reuters on Wednesday said that Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke's shock rise in interest rates would be the last before an election.</p>
<p>Economists, surveyed after Clarke upped base rates to 6.0 percent from 5.75 percent, were also asked where base rates would be at end-1997 and where the peak of the interest rate cycle would be.</p>
<p>Following are the full results of the survey.</p>
<p>				  BASE RATES	  PEAK OF INTEREST</p>
<p>				  AT END-1997	 RATE CYCLE</p>
<p> Median forecast	    6.75		  7.00</p>
<p> Highest forecast	   8.50		  8.50</p>
<p> Lowest forecast	    6.25		  6.25</p>
<p> No of forecasts	    20		    19</p>
<p> ABN-AMRO		     6.50		  N/F</p>
<p> Bank of America	    6.75		  7.00</p>
<p> Bankers Trust Co	   7.00		  7.50</p>
<p> Charterhouse		 8.50		  8.50</p>
<p> Credit Lyonnais	    7.25		  7.50</p>
<p> CS First Boston	    6.75		  7.00</p>
<p> Deutsche Morgan Grenfell 7.25		  8.00</p>
<p> DKB International	  6.25		  6.25</p>
<p> HSBC James capel	   6.75		  7.25</p>
<p> Julius Baer		  7.00		  7.00</p>
<p> Lloyds Bank		  6.75		  7.50</p>
<p> Natwest Group		7.25		  7.25</p>
<p> Nikko Europe		 6.75		  7.00</p>
<p> Paine Webber		 6.75		  7.00</p>
<p> San Paolo Bank	     6.50		  7.00</p>
